          "id": "india-delhi-smog-diwali-2026-11-09",
          "headline": "Thick smog covers Delhi after Diwali fireworks; AQI above 350 in many areas",
          "summary": "Delhi woke up to heavy smog on Monday after firecrackers were burst through Sunday evening despite Supreme Court limits that allowed only green crackers for set hours. The Air Quality Index crossed 350 in several parts of the city. Delhi minister Kapil Mishra says stubble burning in Punjab rose tenfold over two days and has asked Punjab's AAP government to file FIRs.",
          "why_it_matters": "Bad air hits the health of over 30 million people and can bring tougher curbs on traffic and building work in the capital.",
          "importance": 3,
          "lead": false,
          "verified": false,
          "note": "Air quality facts single source: Al Jazeera (AFP/AP). Punjab stubble-burning figure is a claim by Delhi minister Kapil Mishra; not independently confirmed.",
