          "id": "currency-rupee-gives-up-gains-2026-11-09",
          "headline": "Rupee touches 93.74 early, then slips back to about 94.08 per dollar",
          "summary": "The rupee opened near 93.85 and rose 24 paise to 93.74 per dollar in early trade, helped by lower crude, foreign buying (FIIs bought Rs 13,750 crore of shares on Friday) and hopes of Middle East peace. By early afternoon it had given up those gains and traded near 94.08, slightly weaker than Friday's 93.98 close. The dollar index was a little softer near 102.",
          "why_it_matters": "The rupee is holding near six-month highs; dealers see 94.40-94.50 as resistance and 93.50 as the next support.",
          "importance": 4,
          "lead": false,
          "verified": false,
          "note": "Early-trade figures from PTI (carried by Business Standard); afternoon level from Yahoo Finance at 1:44 PM IST.",
